  "final": "`get_document` and `list_documents` now enforce tenant, owner, and `deleted_at IS NULL`. The public check and a new security check both pass.\n\n**Changes**\n\n- **`src/repository.py`**: `find` and `listing` now take `tenant` and `owner` and filter on them along with `deleted_at IS NULL`. `find` also matches on `id`. All values are passed as bound parameters, so names containing quotes are safe. `listing` orders by `id`. Returned dicts still contain only `id`, `title`, and `body`.\n- **`src/service.py`**: `get_document` and `list_documents` pass `tenant` and `owner` through to the repository. Their signatures are unchanged.\n- **`checks/security.py`** (new): covers cross-tenant, cross-owner, and soft-deleted IDs all returning `None`, owners and titles containing quotes, injection-style tenant and owner strings returning nothing, id ordering in lists, and that results contain only the three fields.\n\n**Verification**\n\n- `python3 checks/public.py`: passes.\n- `python3 checks/security.py`: passes.\n\nThe existing `find` and `listing` signatures changed. Nothing else in the repo calls them.",
